Usage: hexdump [OPTION]... [FILE]...

Display file contents in hexadecimal, decimal, octal, or ascii.

The hexdump utility is a filter which displays the specified files,
or standard input, in a user-specified format.

Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.

  -b               one-byte octal display
  -c               one-byte character display
  -C               canonical hex+ASCII display
  -d               two-byte decimal display
  -e FORMAT        format string
  -f FORMAT_FILE   format file
  -n LENGTH        interpret only LENGTH bytes of input
  -o               two-byte octal display
  -s OFFSET        skip OFFSET bytes from the beginning
  -v               display all input, no squeeze
  -x               two-byte hex display

OPTIONS:
  -b             one-byte octal display
  -c             one-byte character display
  -C             canonical hex+ASCII display
  -d             two-byte decimal display
  -o             two-byte octal display
  -x             two-byte hex display
  -e ARG         format string
  -f ARG         format file
  -n ARG         interpret only LENGTH bytes of input
  -s ARG         skip offset bytes from the beginning
  -v             display all input, no squeeze
  -L, --color    interpret color formatting specifiers
      --help     display this help and exit
  -V, --version  output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
